  "problem": "The table below gives the values of $x$ that satisfy $P(X\\ge x)=p,$ where $X∼{χ}^{2}(k).$ Given that $X∼{χ}^{2}(5),$ find the value of $x$ such that $P(X<x)=0.01.$\n\n| $k∖p$ | $0.995$ | $0.990$ | $0.975$ | $0.950$ | $0.900$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $3$ | $\\,0.072\\,$ | $\\,0.115\\,$ | $\\,0.216\\,$ | $\\,0.352\\,$ | $\\,0.584\\,$ |\n| $4$ | $\\,0.207\\,$ | $\\,0.297\\,$ | $\\,0.484\\,$ | $\\,0.711\\,$ | $\\,1.064\\,$ |\n| $5$ | $\\,0.412\\,$ | $\\,0.554\\,$ | $\\,0.831\\,$ | $\\,1.145\\,$ | $\\,1.610\\,$ |",
